{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018KBj9w9vkScWgjz83KhNKi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the design data. Let me also check:\n1. The design uses \"Questrial\" font - I need to install @fontsource/questrial\n2. Check the images folder for any existing images\n3. Check src/content/ for any existing files\n\nLet me now plan my implementation:\n\n## Sections Checklist:\n1. Demo Banner\n2. Navigation\n3. Divider\n4. Hero Section\n5. Product Lines\n6. Fragrances Section (7 fragrances)\n7. How to Order (3 steps)\n8. Brand Story\n\n\n9. Good to Know (3 cards - design only has 3 in gtkGrid, not 4)\n10. Footer\n11. WhatsApp Floating Button\n\nI also need to update the design tokens with the color palette (#1A1A1A for primary, #763B13 for secondary, #C4A882 for accent, plus the supporting colors and #25D366 for WhatsApp) and confirm the typography setup with Questrial for headings and Libre Baskerville for display text.\n\nNow I'm looking at the image situation - the design uses AI-generated images but I have real product photos in the assets folder that I should use instead, including the owner photo. My plan is to install the Questrial font, set up all the design tokens in global CSS, create the content JSON files, copy assets to the public folder, build out the components, and then assemble everything into the final page.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1138,"cache_read_input_tokens":57259,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1138},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"05E79F4F-0A3E-45E4-9EE6-1F04D5D200A4","uuid":"4916280d-c602-4117-a452-ed5438e4fdb2"}
